* text=auto eol=crlf
*.sh !eol

# ClonkMars and Eke Reloaded retain their imported byte conventions even though
# this repository maintains derivative working trees. Keep Git from rewriting
# unchanged bytes: eol normalization would move resource and network checksums.
/ClonkMars.c4d/** binary
/ClonkMars.c4f/** binary
/EkeReloaded.c4d/** binary
/EkeReloaded.c4f/** binary

# Same reasoning for the packs taken from CCAN.
# These ship a mixture of CRLF and LF files; normalizing rewrote roughly half
# of Metal & Magic's bytes on the first commit attempt, which would have
# changed every group checksum away from the imported baseline a non-clonk-rs
# peer may be running. Preserve bytes unless a reviewed change intends otherwise.
/MetalMagic.c4d/** binary
/MetalMagicExtra.c4d/** binary
/Melees.c4f/Queron3.c4s/** binary

# The Ultimate Clonk Compilation v3.0 curation and the dependency packs it
# needs. Same reasoning again: preserve their imported byte conventions and do
# not let checkout normalization rewrite unchanged files.
#
# Collection.c4f holds packed .c4s scenarios next to plain Folder.txt/Title.txt/
# Desc*.rtf files. Without this rule the eol=crlf default would normalise those
# text files on staging and move the bytes of a pack we do not own.
/Collection.c4f/** binary

# E.P.I.C. is distributed the same way: its scenario folder is exploded so the
# sweep sees every .c4s, while its definition pack remains packed inside it.
/E.P.I.C.c4f/** binary

# Exploded into directories rather than left as single packed files: cargo xtask
# scenario-sweep walks the filesystem, so a packed .c4f hides every scenario
# inside it from the sweep. MissionsHarkon.c4f is exploded for a second reason —
# at 105 MB packed it exceeds GitHub's per-file push limit.
/Golems.c4f/** binary
/ModernCombat.c4f/** binary

# Left packed, one file each. A packed group returns its stored header order,
# which is host-stable and is what C++ C4MaterialMap::Load consumes, where an
# unpacked directory would return unsorted readdir order.
/Collection.c4f/Adventures.c4f/InExantros.c4f/INEXSzenarioObjekte.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Adventures.c4f/InExantros.c4f/InExantros.C4D binary
/Collection.c4f/Fun.c4f/ClonkPartyRes.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Fun.c4f/ClonkPartyRes2.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Fun.c4f/GIDL_Race.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Fun.c4f/Zombieland.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Fun.c4f/Zombiesounds.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Hazard.c4f/Jetbelt.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Hazard.c4f/PhysGun.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Magus.c4f/Clonkrix-Remake.c4f/Clonkrix.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Magus.c4f/KdD_Magie_Pack.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/ModernCombat.c4f/BlacksCMC-Waffenmod.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Puzzles.c4f/Explorer.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Races.c4f/Clinfinity.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Races.c4f/Ropepack.c4d binary
/Collection.c4f/Settling.c4f/RufDerWipfeRE.c4f/RufDerWipfe.c4d binary
/Golems.c4d binary
/ModernCombat.c4d binary
/RopepackRemake.c4d binary
/WesternBalancing.c4d binary
/WesternBugfixes.c4d binary

# Repository infrastructure, not game content. Keep it at LF: the eol=crlf rule
# above is there to preserve pack bytes, and it would otherwise reach the shell
# scripts embedded in the workflows and the test scripts beside them.
#
# Written as the whole directory rather than file by file, because the previous
# form named publish-content.yml specifically and a second workflow added later
# silently fell back to CRLF.
/.github/** text eol=lf
